--
-- Driver shifts and location telemetry (DEL-5 plan 2.1; data §2.2, §6, §10; domain model §3.6,
-- §3.7, §3.17, §7; ADR-0009, ADR-0025, ADR-0028, ADR-0031). Four tenant tables with the template
-- policies of 0003, enabled by core_enable_tenant_rls() when the job runs with ELX_RLS=on; the ring
-- and head rows carry account_id for RLS like every operational row. del_driver_shifts: one live
-- (active or paused) shift per driver by the partial unique index. del_driver_locations: the ring
-- of 240 points per driver, PK (driver_id, slot), update-heavy, so fillfactor 70 for heap-only
-- updates and per-table autovacuum at 2 % (data §6). del_driver_location_heads: the ring head and
-- the latest point. del_driver_trails: one LineStringM per driver and business day (M = Unix
-- seconds), GiST on the path, the worker's scan index on business_date. Grants: elx_app keeps the
-- default SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE of 0001 (the driver and staff doors; the worker's jobs
-- write per account in elx_app transactions); elx_platform may only read them (cross-tenant scans,
-- the console's reads of wave 2). Positions are personal data of the driver (data §10): pii:driver.
